{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1381578-alternative-touchstones-and-morality-homebrew","id":1381578,"title":"Alternative Touchstones and Morality Homebrew","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-15T02:54:10-07:00","id":1381578,"title":"Alternative Touchstones and Morality Homebrew","content":"I\u2019ve been working on what has turned out to be a *very* sizable Homebrew! This goes into detail about Touchstones and convictions in play, but more importantly covers a method for introducing non Mortal touchstones to your game as well as Sabbat paths and the like \u2013 there are a significant amount of loresheets to go with them as well. As a loose summary this document contains:<ul><li>\u201cHumanity\u201d for immoral vampires</li> <li>Alternative types of Touchstones</li> <li>The Paths of Enlightenment</li> <li>Loresheets for the Paths</li> <li>Example Tenets and Convictions</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1N7z5WJa4WcghanB-mSGqdqIymRB7vteu\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1N7z5WJa4WcghanB-mSGqdqIymRB7vteu\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1N7z5WJa4WcghanB-mSGqdqIymRB7vteu\" target=\"_blank\"> https://drive.google.com/open?id=1N7z5WJa4WcghanB-mSGqdqIymRB7vteu </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24788-chipotlechris","name":"chipotlechris","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24788_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T03:27:12-07:00","id":1381587,"title":"","content":"I like this. I especially like your reworked version of Feral Heart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T03:52:43-07:00","id":1381595,"title":"","content":"Glad you liked it! As you can see, there\u2019s a fair amount of work gone into all! The Feral Heart loresheet is one of my favourites as well, especially the 5 dot frenzy capabilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24788-chipotlechris","name":"chipotlechris","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24788_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T04:52:10-07:00","id":1381606,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I actually can't wait to try this out. :-D","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T11:08:32-07:00","id":1381706,"title":"","content":"This is really great! I had a similar thought for how to handle Paths when V5 first came out but I was mostly focusing on Path of the Bones. Really great work here!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The only consistent wisdom is in knowing you know nothing&quot; ~ Socrates <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1197-imthestein","name":"Imthestein","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1197_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T11:32:26-07:00","id":1381714,"title":"","content":"Glad you like it! What do you all make of the Beast Marks mechanic? My idea stemmed from paths always making you appear as if you had low humanity score despite your score, and even the virtues of conviction and instinct affecting how you related to stimulus and even frenzy. <br /> <br /> Anyone have a favourite path based on this? Would you use it in game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24788-chipotlechris","name":"chipotlechris","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24788_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T18:19:53-07:00","id":1381838,"title":"","content":"I like the Beast Marks. It's a good way to symbolize the alienness of paths. I also like your alternate names for &quot;Humanity&quot;. Every version of morality being called &quot;Humanity&quot; in 5th gives me the bitter lemon face.<br /> <br /> The only thing I'd change is the first loresheet for Feral Heart. Many Gangrel wouldn't have the Haven merit, using earthmeld instead. Meaning the first dot of Feral Heart is worthless to the clan most likely to be on Feral Heart.<br /> <br /> Maybe change it to something more universal for a Feral Hearter, like once a story you automatically succeed on a hunting roll, or once a story you don't need to make a rouse check to use Animalism. Or just dump the &quot;you must have an existing Haven to gain benefit from this&quot; part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","user":"CajunKhan","date":". 04-16-2020, 01:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T22:45:42-07:00","id":1381863,"title":"","content":"Death of Body and Soul 5 only give the ability to kill someone to regain 1wp?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T22:53:14-07:00","id":1381864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1381578-alternative-touchstones-and-morality-homebrew?p=1381863#post1381863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Death of Body and Soul 5 only give the ability to kill someone to regain 1wp?</div> </div> </div> </div>One aggravated willpower damage, and it ghost servant that is guaranteed at your beck and call. Which given that aggravated willpower only heals if a character has either: Acted in a way to benefit their touchstone significantly, upheld a conviction against their best interest, or if they actively worked towards an ambition (The last one is only at the end of a session) it's a pretty powerful merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24893,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24893-necroticbinder","user":"Necroticbinder","date":". 04-16-2020, 01:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24893-necroticbinder","name":"Necroticbinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T23:40:55-07:00","id":1381865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Necroticbinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1381578-alternative-touchstones-and-morality-homebrew?p=1381864#post1381864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One aggravated willpower damage, and it ghost servant that is guaranteed at your beck and call. Which given that aggravated willpower only heals if a character has either: Acted in a way to benefit their touchstone significantly, upheld a conviction against their best interest, or if they actively worked towards an ambition (The last one is only at the end of a session) it's a pretty powerful merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not see my players wasting precious xp only to do that, but to each their own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-16T00:37:00-07:00","id":1381870,"title":"","content":"Very good work! I'll probably use this in my game. Beast marks is a great idea. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25915-nicolai","name":"nicolai","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-16T04:38:57-07:00","id":1381891,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3598_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3598\" data-vbnamecard=\"3598\">CajunKhan</a> thanks for the feedback. The logic behind needing a Haven for this merit was so that someone couldn't take the No Haven flaw and use this to get around it. my idea was that as it's primarily Sabbat on this path, there was likely a Pack or communal Haven they had, even if it was rarely used. Here they are allowed to roam and do what they want with an extra level of security - essentially they know spots that are good to look for and are safe. I suspect plenty of STs will handwave the haven requirement if it's an issue though.<br /> <br /> With regards to Death and Soul 5, as was pointed out above you also get a temporary ally that is pretty killer as well as have the ability to remove Compulsions that are effecting you. For the Agg Willpower - in my experience it can be Hell to recover from Aggravated WP damage, especially if it racks up. I appreciate it won't be for everyone, but ultimately i'm of the feeling that most people won't get every part of a Loresheet anyway and will pick and choose what fits them.<br /> <br /> I love the Metamorphosis 5 dot power for example - but its a very niche power to need to use. it's evocative and cool however so felt fitting enough<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24788-chipotlechris","name":"chipotlechris","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24788_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-16T05:09:18-07:00","id":1381899,"title":"","content":"Edit: changed my mind about some stuff, making this post no longer in line with my current perspective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","user":"CajunKhan","date":". 05-12-2021, 02:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.co